{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310641,"nonce":"XqaVnPePT5zjkmhH8/0X7CdwoDs=","title":"LLVM's same-name declaration reuse compared user parameters against a full parameter list, and only the unconditional env parameter was ...","message":"`declare_function` in `compiler/src/codegen/llvm_jit_backend.rs` reuses an\nexisting LLVM declaration when a same-named function \"has a matching\nsignature\". It built `expected_params` from `function.signature.parameters`\nalone — no sret, no env — and compared it against `existing_func`'s **full**\nLLVM parameter list.\n\nThat comparison is between a shorter list and a longer one, and it was only ever\ncorrect by accident: while every non-extern Haxe function was declared\n`[i64 env, ...user]`, `expected.len()` (N) could never equal `existing.len()`\n(N+1), so same-named functions always fell through to a unique `name_\u003cid\u003e`\nsymbol. Narrowing the env rule makes N == N, the reuse fires, and two distinct\nfunctions **collapse onto one LLVM FunctionValue** — only the first body is\nemitted and calls to the second run the first's code. Silent wrong code.\n\nFixed by building `expected_params` with the same hidden-parameter prologue the\ndeclaration itself uses.\n\n**The general lesson, which cost several hours:** a hidden parameter that is\nalways present is load-bearing in places that never mention it. Before removing\none, grep for every arity comparison — `len() ==`, `count_params()`,\n`num_llvm_params == num_ir_args + 1` — because each is a latent decision that\nthe constant prefix was silently disambiguating.\n\nTwo more sites of exactly this shape, both fixed by recording the truth instead\nof re-deriving it:\n- `compile_direct_call` inferred sret-vs-env from argument arity. A call that\n  omits a trailing defaulted argument to a receiver-first method reads as an\n  sret call, invents an sret slot, and shifts every argument.\n- `compile_function_body` bound parameters from a rule applied a second time,\n  while `declare_function` has ~13 `function_map.insert` sites and several\n  **reuse** an existing symbol without going near that rule.\n\nBoth now read `hidden_prefix: BTreeMap\u003cIrFunctionId, usize\u003e`, written by\n`bind_declaration` at every one of those sites as\n`declared_params - non_void_user_params`.\n\nSee [[bugs_benchmark_preset_never_reaches_llvm]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_llvm_declaration_reuse_collapses_functions` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}